; =====================================================================
; errata-6543-proposal.abnf
;
; VERBATIM.  The change Erratum ID 6543 PROPOSED and RFC 9682 DID NOT
; TAKE, as RFC 9682 reproduces it.  Copied unchanged; NOT authored by
; this project.
;
; Locator:  RFC 9682, "Updates to the Concise Data Definition Language
;           (CDDL) Grammar", C. Bormann, November 2024, Standards
;           Track, ISSN 2070-1721.  Updates: 8610.
;           <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9682.txt>
;
; Source digest (sha256 of the full cached source text):
;   d35602e7f784e509a5984283ea8d998adfee23f086ad0d77bd22f98c6cdea89c
;
; Appendix B.1, "Change Proposed by Erratum ID 6543" (Figure 13: Proposal
; from Erratum ID 6543 to Split the Byte String Rules).  Source lines
; 616-620.  Appendix B is INFORMATIVE -- its opening line, quoted:
; "This appendix is informative."
;
; THIS GRAMMAR IS NOT IN FORCE AND NEVER WAS.  It is kept because it is
; the only record of the alternative, and because the reason it was
; declined is a design finding: the proposal routes the content of a
; prefixed byte string through QCHAR -> WS -> NL -> COMMENT -> PCHAR,
; and PCHAR admits an apostrophe, so a comment inside an h'' literal
; could carry an unescaped single quote.  RFC 9682 states the
; consequence (source lines 625-626): "This potentially causes a subtle
; change, which is hidden in the WS rule".
;
; WHAT WAS DONE INSTEAD, Appendix B.2, quoted (source lines 658-662):
; "This document takes the simpler approach of leaving the processing of
; the content of the byte string literal to a semantic step after
; processing the syntax of the bytes and BCHAR rules, as updated by
; Figures 2 and 4 in Section 2.1".
;
; The grammar in force is cddl-updated.abnf.
; =====================================================================

; ---- BEGIN VERBATIM FIGURE-13 (the declined split of the byte-string rules) (source lines 616-620, sha256 98d7f3a675126927ab546277adb0937589f008d6c8e130462453f011dac0d428) ----
   ; Proposal from Erratum ID 6543:
   bytes = %x27 *BCHAR %x27
         / bsqual %x27 *QCHAR %x27
   BCHAR = %x20-26 / %x28-5B / %x5D-10FFFD / SESC / CRLF
   QCHAR = DIGIT / ALPHA / "+" / "/" / "-" / "_" / "=" / WS
; ---- END VERBATIM FIGURE-13 (the declined split of the byte-string rules) ----
